	title = {From {{Chaos}} to {{Order}}},
	abstract = {In the previous chapter we have discussed the notion of time as absolute flux. In this chapter, we will discuss the opposite notion, namely, which denies any spatial contamination of time so that duration is only an intensity of feeling put forward by Bergson. With the juxtaposition of these two notions of time, the purpose of this chapter is to see whether and how there can be some sort of mediation between two extremes so that we can work out a certain structure of temporal flow by means of language.},
